The MIDI package is based on libADLMIDI by Vitaly Novichkov and adlmidi
by Joel Yliluoma, and uses DMXOPL definitions by Shannon Freeman. Source
file headers contain copyright information. The package is licensed under
the GNU LGPL, version 2.1 or later; see LICENCE.

The embedded adlmidi.dat contains instrument banks. Available upstream
license texts and provenance notes for bank sources are retained in
notices/. These include notices for AIL, DMXOPL, FMSynth, IMF90,
The Fat Man's tone libraries and O'Connell's IBK files.

The locally available generator configuration includes bank sources in
the upstream greyzone directory. The upstream note in notices/ explains
that permission for those sources is unclear. The exact provenance and
licensing of every instrument in the embedded database have not been
verified; the retained notices do not resolve those questions.

The MIDI package also depends on pcm and opl3, which include code licensed
under the GNU LGPL, version 2.1 or later. See ../pcm/LICENCE and
../opl3/LICENCE. Binary distributors should review the applicable license
terms for the code and banks included in their distribution.
